  "worked_solution": "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $5\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+5\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-5\\text{i},$ or simply $-5\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-5\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{5\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{5\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-5\\text{i}}{-5\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-25\\text{i}-10{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-25{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-25\\text{i}-10(-1)}{-25(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10-25\\text{i}}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10-25\\text{i}}{25} & =\\frac{10}{25}-\\frac{25}{25}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
